## Rows skipped (with reason)

- **cs-a 11 and cs-b 12 — space thousands separators ("500 000", "1 579 589").** ACCEPTED-ROUND skips these, and `NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.cs` in scripts/check-column-translation.mjs line 685 is `'dot'`. Every dotted amount was left byte-identical. Same decision as rounds 1–4.
- **cs-a 12 — the spare "1" in "za poslední 1 rok", "méně než 1 rok", "na 1 měsíc", "za 1 den", "pro 1 poškozeného a 1 nehodu", "1 osobu", "dokončený 1 rok".** `SMALL_LEXICON_WORDS` (line 1782) has no `cs` entry, so Czech "jeden rok" is not counted; dropping the digit makes the number `missing from translation`, which is a hard FAIL of the `numbers` check. Digits kept. Where the same phrase also had a grammatical defect the grammar was fixed with the digit in place (cs-b 52 "po dobu 1 roku", cs-b 43 "s výpovědní dobou 30 dní", cs-b 18 "asi 10 odvětví", cs-b 46 "do 3 měsíců").
- **cs-a 13 and cs-b 19 — U+200B blank lines and the 005 `**​**` lines; promoting 003 Q16–Q20 to headings.** Verified byte-for-byte against the Korean source: `src/content/columns/003` has ZWSP-only lines at exactly the same 52 line numbers as `columns-cs/003`, and 005 (8), 013 (4), 015 (3) likewise. `checkBlocks` compares block count AND a separate `ZWSP` count against the source, and `checkHeadings` compares the heading level list; deleting a ZWSP or promoting Q16 fails. The reviewer is right that lines 58/72/86/108 of 013 render as empty paragraphs, but it is a source-pipeline artifact shared by de/fr/pl, not a Czech defect — it belongs to the supervisor, not to this lane. Wherever a row asked for a merge or split, the text was redistributed **inside** the existing blocks instead (cs-a 17, cs-a 18, cs-a 8, cs-b 20+21).

