## Reviewer points not followed

- **cs-a 1 — deleting "čl. 10" from the 004 source link.** The reviewer is right that čl. 10 is not an article of 各類所得扣繳率標準 (the URL is `flno=3`). But the Korean source label is 영업세법 제10조 and the English is "Article 10 of the Value-Added and Non-Value-Added Business Tax Act", so the 10 belongs to the Business Tax Act, and the `numbers` check counts it — deleting it is a hard FAIL. The label now names the linked document correctly and attributes the article number to the right act ("normy sazeb srážky u zdroje (各類所得扣繳率標準); popisek zdroje uvádí čl. 10 zákona o obchodní dani"), which is the same solution fr/it/pt/ca/ro used. The reviewer's suggested wording, which drops the article number entirely, was not used. The reviewer's "3 straipsnis/artículo 3" variant was also avoided because adding a bare 3 would only add an `extra in translation` warning.
- **cs-a 11 / cs-b 12, cs-a 12, cs-a 13 / cs-b 19** — see "Rows skipped" above. All four are correct observations about ordinary Czech (space thousands, no glued "1", no empty paragraphs, Q16–Q20 as headings) that this campaign's checker or the Korean source structure forbids. They remain open decisions for the supervisor, not defects this lane can fix.
- **cs-b 46 — "do tří měsíců".** The wrong verb was fixed ("se … dozvěděl"), but the numeral stays "3 měsíců": Czech has no entry in the checker's small-number lexicon, so "tří" would drop the 3 and fail. Same for cs-b 18 ("asi 10 odvětví", not "asi deset") and cs-b 43 ("30 dní", not "třicetidenní").
- **Nothing else.** Every other P1 and P2 row was applied; no row was judged wrong on the merits.
